n you factor  in inflation it becomes about eighty two  dollars worth of buying power in ten  years time the fetish is really trying  to get people to spend their money that  doesn't mean that mortgage rates will go  to zero percent but it is a rate that  banks and institutions like that can  borrow from and so other interest rates  do follow  long and will lower when the feds funds  rate drops and will raise when the  federated Rises this isn't the first  time the rate has gone to 0% in fact  during the 2008 financial crisis the  rate was cut to a sliver above 0% and  stayed there for 8 years this is one of  the feds big tools it's its biggest tool  however when the Fed did it during the  financial crisis rates were above 5  percent so the difference for a consumer  who had money in the bank or who was  looking at bonds whereas the stocks are  saving for suspending that's a huge  difference making 5 percent on your  money versus making nothing but when the  Fed cut the rate to 0 on Sunday doll  futures plummeted now the Dow is a  basket of 30 stocks across various  industries meant to reflect the overall  economy if the Dow is up it's meant to  be viewed as a sign that the economy is  doing well if it's down there may be  trouble ahead Dow futures are used when  the market isn't open to predict what  the market might open act when the Fed  cut the rate to zero Dow futures plunged  5% and on Monday morning it went down  even further if an interest rate of zero  is a good thing why did it go down so  much we're coming from a 1 percent rate  which means that it's not as big of a  thing for investors usually when rates  are cut that leads the stock market to  rise but that didn't happen this time  which means one of two things people  expect rates to be cut and then they are  cut usually nothing happens or if  they're cut less than the market  expected  there's nowhere more it could have gone  so the other thing is that the Fed this  is something that we've been worrie